  "term": "International Classification of Diseases",
  "definition": "The International Classification of Diseases is a worldwide system for coding and classifying diagnoses and health conditions in healthcare records. Its tenth revision, ICD-10, is widely used to organize health data for reporting, research, policy, planning, and related administrative purposes such as billing and claims processing.",
